      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PLAY IT COOL (5) has had plenty of chances but does look close to an elusive win after charging home late to be beaten under a length over 1618m at Coffs Harbour last start. Beautifully weighted under today's scale and is drawn to enjoy an economical run. SO SAIN (6) is also a long-term maiden but is racing well with three consecutive minor placings, the latest when stretched to 1700m at Grafton. In the money at both tries over this distance. Should be in the finish again. SARMAT (2) settled a long way back before making late ground to finish fourth when resuming over 1200m at Grafton recently. Has only raced twice so there is plenty of improvement in store, particularly out to this sort of trip. AIRHAWK (1) has been strong through the line in his two starts to date, both over shorter journeys. Gets his chance to shine at this more suitable trip. PRESTIGE EXOTIC (8) is another lightly raced conveyance who can improve with a step up in distance today.",
